## 4. Review gates for the proposal (checkable conditions; each gate cites its bench fact)

- **G1 Coordinate identity separation.** The proposal must define four distinct things — stored observation coordinates (+ per-record CRS/units metadata), displayed map coordinates (rendering-space transform), geometry/edit identity (stable record/revision ids), exported coordinates (per-export transform receipt) — and must state that the display path never writes back. Basis: V1, V4. *A proposal that blurs "the pin showed the right place" with "the export is correct" fails the brief.*
- **G2 Unknown/ambiguous CRS metadata gate.** Imports with missing, ambiguous, or non-registry CRS/units must land in an explicit bounded correction/import choice, storing WKT2 (not a lossy proj-string) and the chosen resolution as provenance. Basis: V4. Auto-guessing (e.g., "if |x|>90 assume lon/lat") is a documented-guess antipattern the brief forbids.
- **G3 Boundary cases are investigated, not universalized.** Antimeridian tracks: segmentation recorded as provenance (V2). Boundary-adjacent queries: rtree 32-bit rounding → expand query boxes / keep authoritative coords in the record table (V6). Incomplete coordinates: `geometry:null` + status + provenance retained (V3). Conflicting identifiers: deterministic precedence + surfaced conflict, never silent overwrite (V7). Each case needs its own validation example; a blanket "we handle all edge cases" claim fails.
- **G4 Merge contract with explicit resolution.** Two-copy divergence must produce: per-record revision chains, union merge for disjoint edits, a surfaced conflict list for same-record edits (both values + author + provenance), and explicit user resolution; OR an append-only operation-log design. No "automatic perfect merge" promise. Basis: V7. Bundle identity must be defined (project UUID + per-copy branch/revision pointer) so re-import of the same source and copy exchange are idempotent and distinguishable.
- **G5 Interrupted-write recovery.** After interrupted save/import/merge, reopen must distinguish committed records from incomplete work. Concrete mechanism [INFER, gated on validation]: SQLite transactions per logical commit + a staging/append journal for multi-step imports/merges + `rtreecheck()`/`PRAGMA integrity_check` on open (V6 for rtreecheck existence; semantics [UNVERIFIED-in-capture]). Failure records stay visible (V3 pattern).
- **G6 Licensing is per-source and pinned.** The proposal must name the actual bundled map source and pin its license terms; ODbL-derived bundles trigger attribution + share-alike on exchange (V9); OSMF tile-server terms remain unverified this stage ([UNVERIFIED] in §2/V9) and offline harvesting from the slippy tile service must not be assumed permitted. No proprietary/licensed data may appear as a default.
- **G7 Scale target honesty.** 250k-observation bounded inspection is an engineering target: rtree + rowid-windowed table access + page-bounded cancellation + streamed export is a plausible architecture within 4 cores/8 GB [INFER from V6], but it is UNMEASURED — the proposal must present it as a target with a proposed benchmark, not a benchmark result.
- **G8 Every derived computation gets its own unit/axis test.** The T1 trail shows a CRS in feet corrupting a scale-factor API while raw transforms worked; T2 shows normalization gaps in 2026 code. Validation plan must include: lat/lon vs lon/lat round trip (V1/V4), feet/metre unit paths (T1), antimeridian segmentation (V2), boundary-window queries (V6), and a two-copy conflict merge scenario (V7) — each as a named, runnable case in the validation plan.

